A '''buff''' is an [[effect]] that can modify an entity's statistics, and can be identified by a green border around its icon.<ref name="IdentifyBuffs" /> Buffs with primarily detrimental effects are ''debuffs'' and have a red border.<ref name="FlaskBuff" />

==Identifying a buff==
[[File:Onslaught buff icon.png|thumb|upright|[[Onslaught]] Buff icon with green border]]
Each buff affecting the player will display an icon with a green border in the top-left of the screen.<ref name="IdentifyBuffs" /><ref name="FlaskBuff" /> This is one way to determine whether or not an effect is a buff - if it does not show an icon, it is not a buff that is attached to the player. 

[[Charge]]s and [[flask]] effects are not considered buffs.

==The functioning of buffs==
A buff adds statistics and modifiers to the creature it is attached to. Although a buff may increase the damage of a affected creature, a buff itself cannot deliver [[hit]]s or take any action. A buff may include degeneration or [[damage over time]] effects. For example, if a monster is attacked by a player using the {{il|Wrath}} aura, the monster is not "hit" by the aura, or the buff, it is the player that hits the monster:
#Wrath is a [[spell]] that is cast by the player.
#The spell creates an [[aura]] that applies a buff to any allies within range.
#The buff contains a [[modifier]] that adds lightning damage to the player's attacks
#The player hits the monster, dealing the added lightning damage

==Buff duration==
All buffs have a [[duration]], which can be infinite (as in the case of [[aura]]s). This duration is affected by {{c|mod|Buff Duration}} modifiers, and may be affected by {{c|mod|Skill Effect Duration}} modifiers if the buff is considered a skill effect.

The passive skills which increase buff and debuff duration apply not to buffs on you but to buffs (including debuffs) you create, either on yourself or other entities. This includes all the above as well as such things as the debuffs placed on cursed monsters.

'''[[Expiration rate|Buff expiration]]''' - Being cursed with {{il|Temporal Chains}} and having the {{stl|Shaper's Presence}} buff can make {{c|mod|Other effects on Cursed enemies expire % slower}}. These 2 mods are additive with one another and capped at 75%.

{{il|Runegraft of the Warp}} provides 30% slower buff expiration rate.
*'''Example''' At 50% {{c|mod|Other effects on Cursed enemies expire % slower}} all buffs expire 2 times slower. This is equivalent to 100% more buff duration for calculating total buff duration.

==Buff effect==
The effect of a buff can also be increased or reduced. Modifiers that increases Buff Effect increase the bonuses from buffs that affect yourself, that includes both positive and negative bonuses. Therefore one has to be careful when amplifying two-sided buffs. 

Currently, the only source of {{c|mod| #% increased Effect of Buffs on you}} comes from {{il|Ichimonji}}. This will for example increase:
*The amount of [[mana regeneration]] granted by the {{il|Clarity}} aura.
*The amount of {{c|mod|Fire Damage per second}} taken by the player using {{il|Righteous Fire}}. It does not increase the amount of {{c|mod|Fire Damage per second}} dealt to enemies since the mod specifies "on you".
*The spell damage bonus provided by a player using {{il|Righteous Fire}}.
*{{il|Blood Rage}} increases the [[life leech]] amount as well as the [[attack speed]] on you, but also increases the total amount of Life and Energy Shields lost.

{{anchor|Debuff}}

===Buff and debuff copies===
* Multiple copies of the same buff do not stack with each other. When multiple copies of the same buff are on one character, the game will only count the strongest buff as active.
* Exceptions are stacking buffs and debuffs such as {{stl|withered}} (stacks upto a limit of 15).

==Debuffs==
A debuff is an [[effect]] that primarily grants a detrimental effect to the debuffed creature and can be identified by having a specific red border around the icon. For instance the damage over time from {{stl|Bleeding}} or {{stl|Poison}} are considered debuffs.<ref name="PunctureDebuff" />

Debuffs on enemies are not generally exposed to the player, though many have audible or visual effects. [[Non-damaging ailment]]s in particular (other than [[freeze]]) display their icon and effect under an affected enemy's life bar.

When a debuffed enemy becomes untargetable, such as bosses in scripted phases, their debuffs are typically hidden, not removed. Their duration (if any) will expire normally, however.<ref>https://imgur.com/4D5c49r</ref> 

Some boss skills can remove debuffs, such as [[Sirus]]' clone summon.

==Related Effects==
The legacy [[Unique Jewel]] {{il|Mantra of Flames}} has the unique mods {{c|mod|Adds (3-5) to (8-12) Fire Attack Damage per Buff on You}} and {{c|mod|Adds (2-3) to (5-8) Fire Spell Damage per Buff on You}}.

